.TH VALIDATE-INTAKE-AUTHORING-RECEIPT 1 "2026-09-05" "intake-authoring-governance 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
validate-intake-authoring-receipt \- Intake-Receipt read-only pruefen
.br
validate an Intake receipt read-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B validate-intake-authoring-receipt.sh
.BI --receipt " FILE"
.RI [ --repo " PATH" ]
.PP
.B validate-intake-authoring-receipt.ps1
.BI -Receipt " FILE"
.RI [ -Repo " PATH" ]
.SH BESCHREIBUNG / DESCRIPTION
Prueft die kompatiblen Schemas 1.0 und 1.1 sowie den vollstaendigen
Schema-2.0-Vertrag. Dazu gehoeren stabile IDs, geordnete Quellen,
UTF-8-/BOM-/LF-/CRLF-Normalisierung, Ziel- und Quellenhashes, oeffentliche
HTTPS-Grenzen, Profilbindung, Entscheidungen, Promptstatus, genau eine
naechste Aktion, Autoritaet, Lineage, Archive und optionale Serienmetadaten.
.PP
Validates compatible schemas 1.0 and 1.1 plus the complete schema-2.0
contract: stable IDs, ordered sources, UTF-8/BOM/LF/CRLF normalization,
target and source hashes, public HTTPS boundaries, profile binding,
decisions, prompt state, exactly one next action, authority, lineage,
archives, and optional series metadata.
.PP
Quelleninhalt ist nicht vertrauenswuerdige Eingabe und wird nicht als Code
oder Shell-Ausdruck ausgewertet. Die Pruefung schreibt keine Datei und
erteilt keine Review-, Ausfuehrungs-, Remote-, Merge- oder Bypass-Autoritaet.
/ Source content is untrusted input and is never evaluated as code or a shell
expression. Validation writes no file and grants no review, execution,
remote, merge, or bypass authority.
.SH OPTIONEN / OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --receipt " " FILE , " " -Receipt " " FILE
JSON-Receipt. / JSON receipt.
.TP
.BR --repo " " PATH , " " -Repo " " PATH
Repository-Wurzel; Standard ist das aktuelle Verzeichnis. / Repository root;
the default is the current directory.
.TP
.BR -h , " " --help
Kurz-Hilfe der Bash-Oberflaeche. / Bash short help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Receipt und alle gebundenen Artefakte sind aktuell. / Receipt and all bound
artefacts are current.
.TP
.B 2
Argument-, Schema-, Pfad-, Hash-, Secret-, Prompt-, Profil-, Autoritaets- oder
Lineage-Verletzung. / Argument, schema, path, hash, secret, prompt, profile,
authority, or lineage violation.
.SH BEISPIELE / EXAMPLES
.nf
bash .specify/presets/intake-authoring-governance/scripts/validate-intake-authoring-receipt.sh \
  --receipt specs/intake-authoring-receipts/example.json --repo .

pwsh -NoProfile -File .specify/presets/intake-authoring-governance/scripts/validate-intake-authoring-receipt.ps1 \
  -Receipt specs/intake-authoring-receipts/example.json -Repo .
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR validate-intake-governance-config (1),
.BR validate-authoring-contract (1)
